# SHACL

```elixir
Mix.install(rudof_elixir: [path: Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)], kino: "== 0.19.0")
```

## Introduction

This document contains a short introduction to [RDF](https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/) using [rudof](https://rudof-project.github.io/). This chapter demonstrates validation with [SHACL](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/).

## Preliminaries: Install and configure rudof

The library is available as `rudof_elixir` from this checkout. First, we install and configure `rudof`; the setup cell installs the Elixir wrapper and creates a native session.

```elixir
alias Rudof.Session
import ExUnit.Assertions
rudof = Session.new!()
```

## Validate using SHACL

Let's read some RDF data.

```elixir
:ok =
  Session.read_data(
    rudof,
    ~S"""
    prefix :       <http://example.org/>
    prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
    prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
    prefix schema: <http://schema.org/>
    prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

    :timbl  rdf:type    :Human ;
            :name       "Tim Berners-Lee" ;
            :birthPlace :london ;
            :birthDate  "1955-06-08"^^xsd:date ;
            :employer   :CERN ;
            :knows      _:1 .
    :london rdf:type    :city, :metropolis ;
            :country    :UK .
    :CERN   rdf:type    :Organization .
    _:1     :birthPlace :Spain .
    """)
```

```elixir
:ok =
  Session.read_shacl(rudof, ~S"""
  prefix :       <http://example.org/>
  prefix sh:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
  prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
  prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
  prefix schema: <http://schema.org/>

  :Person a sh:NodeShape ;
   sh:targetClass :Human ;
   sh:property [ sh:path :name ;
                 sh:datatype xsd:string;
                 sh:minCount 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
   sh:property [ sh:path :birthDate ; sh:datatype xsd:date;
                                      sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
   sh:property [ sh:path :birthPlace ;
                 sh:node :Place; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
   sh:property [
      sh:path :employer ;
      sh:node :Organization
  ] .

  :Place a sh:NodeShape .
  :Organization a sh:NodeShape .
  """)
```

```elixir
{:ok, results} = Session.validate_shacl(rudof)
IO.inspect(results)
assert results.conforms
results
```

The previous data didn't have errors. We can add some data with errors like the following:

```elixir
:ok =
  Session.read_data(
    rudof,
    ~S"""
    prefix :       <http://example.org/>
    prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
    prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
    prefix schema: <http://schema.org/>
    prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

    :wrong1 rdf:type    :Human ;
            :name       "John" ;
            :birthDate  "1955-06-08"^^xsd:date, "1956-06-08"^^xsd:date .
    :wrong2 rdf:type    :Human ;
            :name       23 ;
            :birthDate  "1955-06-08"^^xsd:date .
    """)
```

```elixir
{:ok, results} = Session.validate_shacl(rudof)
IO.inspect(results)
refute results.conforms
assert length(results.results) >= 2
results
```

## Close the session

Release the native state when finished. To revisit earlier cells, evaluate from the beginning.

```elixir
:ok = Session.close(rudof)
```
